# JudeanFloraV1; canonical UE cm (X east, +Y south, Z up), written with Y reflected and triangle winding reversed for the legacy OBJ importer adapter. One o object, no g groups, so the importer creates exactly one material slot.
# Jerusalem pine (Pinus halepensis), LOD2 leaf
# height range 10.0-20.0 m, crown 5.0-9.0 m; source: Zohary & Feinbrun-Dothan, Flora Palaestina vols I-IV (Israel Academy of Sciences, 1966-1986), species entry Pinus halepensis; 10-20 m in the Judean hills, taller only on deep soil
# part kinds and their winding checks are recorded in vegetation-manifest.json
o SM_JudeanFloraV1_JerusalemPine_L2_Leaf
s off
